# Root-level build context .dockerignore - needed because
# backend/Dockerfile builds from the repo root now (it needs to COPY in
# two sibling directories, prompts/ and mcp-gateway/configs/, that live
# outside backend/ itself - see backend/Dockerfile's own comment on why).
# Without this, the entire monorepo (both services' node_modules, git
# history, build artifacts) gets sent as build context on every build -
# slow, and backend/Dockerfile's own `COPY backend/. .` would otherwise
# copy a stale local node_modules/dist straight into the image, silently
# overwriting what RUN npm ci/npm run build just correctly produced
# inside the container - the exact bug class this file exists to prevent.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
coverage
**/coverage
.git
.env
**/.env
**/.env.local
*.log
**/*.log
.DS_Store
.ai
.claude
